# 2. Generate Report — Component Section Smart Filters & Switches

## Background

The Generate Report page includes a Component Section that can display 100–200+ components after team and story selection. Users currently must scroll through the entire list to identify problematic components. There is no way to quickly isolate components by status, filter out valid ones, or bulk-exclude a group.

## Problem Statement

With 100+ components, the component list is unnavigable. Users cannot efficiently identify issues, act on groups of components, or exclude components in bulk. Validation logic before Generate Report must still run on the complete unfiltered dataset.

## ⚠️ Critical Rule

> **Filters are display-only. They NEVER affect the pre-report validation logic.**
> Validation always runs on the complete set of components, regardless of what the user has filtered in or out on screen.
> Existing validation behavior must not change.

## Functional Requirements

### Filter Bar Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-2.1 | Add a **Filter Bar** above the component list in the Component Section. |
| FR-2.2 | The filter bar must include the filter options described below. |
| FR-2.3 | Filters operate on the **currently rendered component list** only — frontend filtering, no new backend calls. |
| FR-2.4 | Multiple filters may be active simultaneously (AND logic — component must match all active filters to be shown). |
| FR-2.5 | A **"Reset All Filters"** button must clear all active filters and restore the full list. |
| FR-2.6 | A **component count** must be shown: `Showing X of Y components`. |
| FR-2.7 | Pre-report validation must continue to evaluate ALL Y components regardless of the active filter. |

### Filter Options

#### Toggle Switches (Quick Filters)

| Switch Label | Shows |
|---|---|
| ✅ Valid Only | Components where Prod K8s matches release branch AND branch cut is complete |
| ❌ Errors Only | Components with at least one error-level validation message |
| ⚠️ Warnings Only | Components with at least one warning-level validation message |
| 🌿 No Branch Formed | Components where no release branch exists matching the current fix version |
| 🔀 Branch Cut Incomplete | Components where branch cut is not yet completed for the fix version |
| 🚫 User Excluded | Components currently marked as User Excluded |
| 📦 Library Components | Components classified as Library type |

#### Dropdown Filters

| Filter | Description |
|---|---|
| Branch Status | All / Has Branch / No Branch / Branch Cut Done / Branch Cut Incomplete |
| Kubernetes Status | All / Deployed & Valid / Deployed & Stale / Not Deployed / Unknown |
| Component Type | All / Service / Library / System Excluded / User Excluded |
| Scrum Team | All / [dynamic list from visible components] |

### Bulk Exclude Feature

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-2.8 | A **checkbox column** must appear on the left of each component row. |
| FR-2.9 | A **Select All (Filtered)** checkbox must select all currently visible (filtered) components. |
| FR-2.10 | A **"Exclude Selected"** button must mark all selected components as User Excluded in one action. |
| FR-2.11 | Excluded components must update their visual state immediately (greyed out / excluded badge). |
| FR-2.12 | A **"Undo Exclusion"** action must be available per component or for the last bulk action. |

## Acceptance Criteria

```
AC-2.1
GIVEN 150 components are loaded
WHEN the user activates the "Errors Only" switch
THEN only components with error-level messages are shown
AND the count reads "Showing X of 150 components"

AC-2.2
GIVEN the "Errors Only" switch is active
WHEN the user also activates "No Branch Formed"
THEN only components matching BOTH conditions are shown (AND logic)

AC-2.3
GIVEN filters are active showing 20 of 150 components
WHEN the user clicks "Generate Report"
THEN validation runs against all 150 components
AND the filter state does NOT affect which components are included in the report

AC-2.4
GIVEN filters are active
WHEN the user clicks "Reset All Filters"
THEN all 150 components are shown
AND all switches and dropdowns return to default state

AC-2.5
GIVEN 20 components are visible after filtering
WHEN the user clicks "Select All (Filtered)" and then "Exclude Selected"
THEN all 20 visible components are marked as User Excluded
AND their visual state updates immediately

AC-2.6
GIVEN the Scrum Team dropdown is open
WHEN the team list is rendered
THEN only teams present in the currently visible (filtered) component rows appear

AC-2.7
GIVEN the "Valid Only" switch is activated
WHEN the filter runs
THEN only components where Prod K8s matches release branch AND branch cut is complete are shown

AC-2.8
GIVEN filters are active and showing a subset
WHEN the component count is viewed
THEN it accurately reads "Showing X of Y components"

AC-2.9
GIVEN a user excludes components via bulk action
WHEN the page is refreshed or report is reopened
THEN the exclusion state is persisted in the database

AC-2.10
GIVEN any filter combination is active
WHEN pre-report validation runs
THEN validation output reflects ALL components and is not scoped to the filtered subset
```

## Edge Cases

- All components match a filter → count reads "Showing Y of Y components", no visual change
- No components match a filter → show empty state: "No components match the selected filters. Reset filters to view all."
- Bulk exclude applied to filtered set → undo only reverses the last bulk action, not previous individual exclusions

