# 6. Deployment Section — Teams & Stories Loading Fix (DB-First Flow)

## Background

When Force Refresh is triggered in the Deployment Section, the backend currently does not load the associated Scrum Teams and Stories for each component. The Teams and Stories columns appear empty in the Deployment table. This is a data flow issue — the backend is not fetching this information from the Components DB table before proceeding with Kubernetes analysis.

## Problem Statement

Teams and Stories are empty because the backend Deployment flow does not query the Component DB records that already contain this information. The fix is to establish a DB-first data load step before any Kubernetes or GitHub analysis begins.

## Correct Backend Flow (Force Refresh)

```
Step 1 — Load Components from DB
  Query Component DB table using:
    - Fix Version
    - Team Key
  Retrieve for each component:
    - Component Name
    - Component Type
    - Associated Scrum Teams
    - Associated Stories
    - Exclusion Status (System / User / None)

Step 2 — Filter Components
  Exclude:
    - Library components
    - System Excluded components
    - User Excluded components
  Only deployable components proceed

Step 3 — Resolve Release Branch
  Reuse existing release calendar resolution service
  No new implementation

Step 4 — Kubernetes Analysis (per component)
  For each deployable component:
    - Fetch running pods from selected Namespace
    - Extract Deployment Labels:
        - K8s Branch Label
        - K8s Commit SHA (full)

Step 5 — GitHub Analysis (per component)
  Fetch release branch commit history ONCE (cache for this request)
  For each component:
    - Find K8s commit SHA on release branch
    - Identify absolute latest commit (including merge commits) → Latest Release Commit ID
    - Count non-merge commits after K8s SHA → Commits Behind

Step 6 — Persist Results
  Save to Deployment Readiness table per component:
    - All fields including Scrum Teams and Stories

Step 7 — Return to UI
  Return full result set including Teams and Stories per component
```

## Functional Requirements

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-6.1 | Step 1 must always execute first — before any K8s or GitHub call. |
| FR-6.2 | Teams and Stories must be loaded from the Component DB record — NOT from iTrack API. |
| FR-6.3 | The Teams and Stories data must be passed through to the Deployment Readiness result and returned to the UI. |
| FR-6.4 | If a component has no teams or stories in DB → return empty list, display `—` in UI. |
| FR-6.5 | If DB has no component records for the given Fix Version → log WARN and show appropriate UI message. |

## Acceptance Criteria

```
AC-6.1
GIVEN Force Refresh is triggered with a valid Fix Version and Namespace
WHEN the backend processes the request
THEN Step 1 (DB component load) executes first
AND Scrum Teams and Stories are loaded from DB before any K8s call

AC-6.2
GIVEN components exist in DB with associated teams and stories
WHEN the Deployment table renders
THEN the Scrum Teams column shows the team names for each component
AND the Stories column shows the story IDs for each component

AC-6.3
GIVEN a component in DB has no associated teams
WHEN the Deployment table renders for that component
THEN the Scrum Teams column shows "—"

AC-6.4
GIVEN a component in DB has no associated stories
WHEN the Deployment table renders for that component
THEN the Stories column shows "—"

AC-6.5
GIVEN the Teams and Stories come from DB
WHEN the backend is processing
THEN NO new iTrack API call is made during Force Refresh

AC-6.6
GIVEN the data flow is corrected
WHEN the Deployment table is fully rendered
THEN all columns (component, teams, stories, K8s branch, commits, status) are populated correctly
```

