# 7. Deployment Section — Branch Comparison Normalization + Status Column Simplification

## Background

### Problem A — Wrong "Older Branch" Status Due to Format Mismatch

The K8s branch label uses **hyphen-separated** format:
```
release-26-07-28-rel
```

The application's release branch uses **slash and dot** format:
```
release/26.07.28.rel
```

Both represent the **same branch**. The current comparison does a raw string equality check and incorrectly reports "Older Branch" when both branches are actually the same.

### Problem B — Two Columns Where One Is Sufficient

The Deployment table shows both a "Commits Behind" column and a "Status" column. The "Commits Behind" count is redundant because the status message can include it. This wastes column space.

## Functional Requirements

### Branch Normalization

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-7.1 | Before any branch comparison, **normalize both branch values to a canonical format**. |
| FR-7.2 | Canonical format: `release/YY.MM.DD.rel` (lowercase, slash separator, dot-separated date parts, `.rel` suffix). |
| FR-7.3 | Normalization must handle the K8s hyphenated format: `release-YY-MM-DD-rel` → `release/YY.MM.DD.rel`. |
| FR-7.4 | Normalization must handle slash/dot format if not already canonical. |
| FR-7.5 | Normalization must be applied at comparison time — the raw stored values in DB remain unchanged. |
| FR-7.6 | The normalization logic must be a shared utility method reusable across the codebase. |
| FR-7.7 | Log both raw and normalized values at DEBUG level during comparison. |

### Normalization Rules

```
Input Formats → Canonical Output

release-26-07-28-rel        →   release/26.07.28.rel
release-26-07-28-release    →   release/26.07.28.rel
release/26.07.28.rel        →   release/26.07.28.rel  (already canonical)
release/26.07.28.release    →   release/26.07.28.rel

Algorithm:
  1. Lowercase the entire string
  2. Extract: YY, MM, DD, suffix
     - Pattern A (hyphens): release-{YY}-{MM}-{DD}-{rel|release}
     - Pattern B (slashes): release/{YY}.{MM}.{DD}.{rel|release}
  3. Normalize suffix: "release" → "rel"
  4. Output: release/{YY}.{MM}.{DD}.rel
```

### Status Column Simplification

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-7.8 | **Remove the "Commits Behind" column** from the Deployment table entirely. |
| FR-7.9 | Keep only a single **"Status"** column. |
| FR-7.10 | The Status column message must convey all information including commit count where relevant. |
| FR-7.11 | Status logic must use normalized branch values for comparison (see FR-7.1 through FR-7.6). |

### Status Message Logic (Priority Order)

```
Priority 1 — Unable to Validate
  Condition:  Release branch could not be resolved
              OR K8s commit not found on release branch
              OR GitHub/K8s fetch failed
  Message:    "Unable to Validate"
  Style:      Grey

Priority 2 — Older Branch
  Condition:  Normalized K8s branch ≠ Normalized resolved release branch
              (Comparison MUST use normalized values — NOT raw strings)
  Message:    "Older Branch"
  Style:      Orange

Priority 3 — X Commits Behind
  Condition:  Normalized branches match
              AND commits_behind > 0 (non-merge commit count)
  Message:    "{N} commit(s) behind. Redeployment recommended."
  Style:      Amber

Priority 4 — Valid
  Condition:  Normalized branches match
              AND commits_behind = 0
  Message:    "Valid"
  Style:      Green
```

## Acceptance Criteria

```
AC-7.1
GIVEN K8s branch label is "release-26-07-28-rel"
AND resolved release branch is "release/26.07.28.rel"
WHEN branch comparison runs
THEN both values are normalized to "release/26.07.28.rel"
AND they are considered EQUAL
AND status is NOT "Older Branch"

AC-7.2
GIVEN K8s branch label is "release-26-07-28-release" (with -release suffix)
WHEN normalization runs
THEN the result is "release/26.07.28.rel"

AC-7.3
GIVEN normalized branches match AND K8s commit SHA = Latest Release commit SHA
WHEN status is determined
THEN status message is "Valid" displayed in green

AC-7.4
GIVEN normalized branches match AND commits_behind = 3
WHEN status is determined
THEN status message is "3 commit(s) behind. Redeployment recommended." in amber

AC-7.5
GIVEN normalized K8s branch does not match normalized release branch
WHEN status is determined
THEN status message is "Older Branch" in orange

AC-7.6
GIVEN the Deployment table renders
WHEN the columns are counted
THEN there is NO "Commits Behind" column
AND only a single "Status" column exists

AC-7.7
GIVEN an unrecognized K8s branch format is encountered
WHEN normalization runs
THEN the raw value is used as-is
AND a WARN is logged with the unrecognized format
AND status is set to "Unable to Validate"

AC-7.8
GIVEN the normalization utility is implemented
WHEN a code review is performed
THEN normalization exists in a single shared utility method
AND is NOT duplicated across multiple comparison sites

AC-7.9
GIVEN the raw K8s branch value is stored in DB
WHEN normalization is applied
THEN the DB stored value remains unchanged (normalization is comparison-time only)
```

