# 9. Deployment Section — Async Performance (ExecutorService + Job ID + DB-Cached Reload)

## Background

The Deployment Section Force Refresh currently executes synchronously, causing the browser to hang while waiting for Kubernetes and GitHub responses. The application already has a well-established async pattern used in Generate Report — this same pattern must be applied to the Deployment Section.

## Problem Statement

1. The Force Refresh hangs the UI while processing 20–100+ components.
2. There is no async job tracking for Deployment analysis.
3. When the user navigates away and returns, data is re-fetched instead of loading from DB.

## Target Behavior

```
User clicks Force Refresh
    ↓
Backend starts async job (returns Job ID immediately)
    ↓
UI receives Job ID → shows progress/loading state
    ↓
Backend processes in parallel (ExecutorService):
    - Load components from DB
    - For each deployable component (parallel):
        - Fetch K8s data
        - Fetch/reuse GitHub commit history
        - Calculate status
    - Persist results to DB
    ↓
UI polls for job completion (or uses existing polling mechanism)
    ↓
Job complete → UI loads results from DB
    ↓
Results displayed in table

User navigates away and returns:
    ↓
UI checks for existing DB records for (Team + Fix Version + Namespace)
    ↓
If records exist → Load from DB immediately (no re-fetch)
    ↓
User can trigger Force Refresh to get fresh data
```

## Functional Requirements

### Async Execution

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-9.1 | **Reuse the existing async job pattern** used in Generate Report — do NOT create a new async framework. |
| FR-9.2 | Force Refresh must return a **Job ID immediately** without blocking. |
| FR-9.3 | Backend must process Deployment analysis in **parallel using ExecutorService** — same executor used for Generate Report. |
| FR-9.4 | Each component's K8s fetch and GitHub analysis must execute in parallel where possible. |
| FR-9.5 | GitHub release branch commit history must be fetched **once per Force Refresh** and shared across all component analyses (existing performance rule). |
| FR-9.6 | Results must be **persisted to DB** as each component completes. |
| FR-9.7 | Job status must be trackable: `IN_PROGRESS`, `COMPLETED`, `FAILED`. |
| FR-9.8 | UI must use the **existing job polling mechanism** — no new polling implementation. |
| FR-9.9 | Maximum execution timeout must be configurable. Default: 120 seconds. |

### DB-Cached Reload

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-9.10 | When the user navigates to the Deployment Section WITHOUT clicking Force Refresh, the UI must **load results from DB** for the selected Team + Fix Version + Namespace. |
| FR-9.11 | The `Last Validated At` timestamp must be displayed so users know how recent the data is. |
| FR-9.12 | A "Stale data" warning must appear if results are older than a configurable threshold (default: 60 minutes). |
| FR-9.13 | Force Refresh always triggers a fresh backend job — never reads from DB cache. |
| FR-9.14 | This DB-cached reload behavior must mirror the existing Review Commits reload behavior exactly. |

### Error Handling

| # | Requirement |
|---|---|
| FR-9.15 | If a single component's K8s or GitHub fetch fails, that component is marked "Unable to Validate" and processing continues for other components — one failure must NOT abort the entire job. |
| FR-9.16 | If the entire job fails, the Job ID is marked `FAILED`, the UI shows an error, and any previously persisted DB results remain available. |

## Acceptance Criteria

```
AC-9.1
GIVEN the user clicks Force Refresh
WHEN the request hits the backend
THEN a Job ID is returned within 500ms
AND the UI transitions to a loading/progress state
AND the browser does NOT hang

AC-9.2
GIVEN the async job is running
WHEN components are processed
THEN K8s and GitHub fetches for multiple components run in parallel
AND the total execution time is substantially less than sequential processing

AC-9.3
GIVEN GitHub commit history is fetched for the release branch
WHEN multiple components are analyzed
THEN GitHub is called only ONCE and the result is reused for all components

AC-9.4
GIVEN the async job completes
WHEN the UI receives the completion signal
THEN results are loaded from DB and displayed in the table
AND "Last Validated At" timestamp is visible

AC-9.5
GIVEN results are in DB from a previous Force Refresh
WHEN the user navigates away and returns to the Deployment Section
THEN previous results load immediately from DB without triggering a new backend job

AC-9.6
GIVEN previously cached results are 90 minutes old
WHEN the user views the Deployment Section
THEN a "Stale data" warning is displayed alongside the Last Validated At timestamp

AC-9.7
GIVEN 1 component out of 30 has a K8s fetch error
WHEN the async job processes components
THEN the 29 other components complete successfully
AND the failed component shows "Unable to Validate"
AND the job status is COMPLETED (not FAILED)

AC-9.8
GIVEN the entire job fails (e.g., K8s cookie expired)
WHEN the failure is detected
THEN the job status is set to FAILED
AND the UI shows a clear error message
AND any previously persisted DB results for this Fix Version remain accessible

AC-9.9
GIVEN the async job is running
WHEN the user clicks Force Refresh again
THEN the previous job is cancelled or a new job supersedes it
AND the UI tracks the latest job ID only

AC-9.10
GIVEN the existing Generate Report async infrastructure is used
WHEN a code review is performed
THEN no duplicate async framework, executor, or job tracking table has been created
